\begin{align*}
8f + 2g &= 932 \\
14f + 3g &= 1402
\end{align*}

We can solve this system using the elimination method. First, we can multiply the first equation by 2 to align the coefficients of $g$:

\begin{align*}
2(8f + 2g) &= 2(932) \\
16f + 4g &= 1864
\end{align*}

Now, we subtract the second equation from this result:

\begin{align*}
(16f + 4g) - (14f + 3g) &= 1864 - 1402 \\
2g &= 462 \\
g &= 231
\end{align*}

Now, we substitute $g = 231$ back into one of the original equations to solve for $f$. Let's use the first equation:

\begin{align*}
8f + 2(231) &= 932 \\
8f + 462 &= 932 \\
8f &= 470 \\
f &= \frac{470}{8} \\
f &= 58.75
\end{align*}

